# Raw HSK 3.0 curriculum source dumps (elkmovie/hsk30, drkameleon, makemeahanzi,
# krmanik grammar) + derived *_import_ready.json staging files -- provenance
# only, not needed at runtime. ~58MB, deliberately untracked.
#
# IMPORTANT (see alembic/versions/06e70a177b1d_...): the assumption that "the
# actual data lives in Postgres" only held for whichever database this was
# manually imported into -- it does NOT reach a fresh database (CI, another
# developer, a freshly deployed server), since backend/scripts/
# import_hsk30_curriculum.py depends on these gitignored files and was only
# ever run by hand, once, locally. That caused a real bug: HSK level pages
# showing "no Hanzi" on any database that only ever got schema migrations.
# The Hanzi dataset specifically now also has a COMMITTED copy at
# backend/alembic/seed_data/hanzi_import_ready.json, inserted automatically
# by that migration on every `alembic upgrade head` -- do not re-gitignore
# that path. Vocabulary/grammar/lesson data still has the same gap and is
# tracked as a separate follow-up, not fixed by this directory rule alone.
backend/data_sources/